# testing=CheckProofsAtRunTime: a cell that the walk still holds as fresh where a function returns is dead there by the walk's own claim, so it is overwritten (EndCellLifetime).
# Code that holds the cell after all crashes the next time it looks into the cell, and the message says where the cell was allocated.
# Fault injection, testing=AssumeCalleesRetainNothing: the walk assumes that the callee of a direct call does not retain an argument, so `o` stays fresh across keep(o).
# No value is wrong: without the check the program prints 3, 3 and continues.
# OPTIONS: testing=CheckProofsAtRunTime,AssumeCalleesRetainNothing
# RUN(CALL): run-in-shell mechanisms=-Inlining
# CALL: bun: internal AOT error: lifetime check failed
# CALL-NEXT: an object that this function allocated was used after the compiler ended its lifetime
# CALL-NOT: went on
# CALL: crashed with
